cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this archive, please cite it and the manuscript it accompanies."
type: software
title: "Code, conditions and aggregate results of 'What moves with the pause definition and the adjustment: a multiverse diagnostic of pause and stall labels in keystroke logs'"
abstract: >-
  A multiverse diagnostic of keystroke pause and stall labels. A window-based stall detector was applied to four
  keystroke datasets released for research (two editions of an introductory programming course, an essay corpus and a
  corpus of writing with model suggestions), its window, threshold, stop condition and segmentation were varied over
  89 definitions around a baseline, and a fixed-threshold pause detector was added; every conclusion is reported with
  an interval from resampling writers. The archive holds the scripts of every computation, the conditions committed
  before each computation (in Japanese, redacted of internal references, with an English summary), the aggregate
  results per definition and the manuscript sources. The data and per-writer values are not included.
